    ["<Assistant_Title1>【Story Mode】</>\n<Assistant_Title2> System Settings: </>Menu-Settings-Camera-Story Mode{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1302534}\n<Assistant_Title2> System Introduction: </>After Story Mode is enabled, the camera will zoom in to a cinematic perspective within story instances to enhance immersion. You can manually toggle it on/off by clicking the switch under the camera button on the bottom left of the screen, or permanently disable it in <Highlight>Settings-Camera-Story Mode-Enable Story Mode Dynamically</>. Once disabled, Story Mode will not activate when entering story instances again (except for some combat scenes).\n<Assistant_Title3> Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Hiding Appearance in Story Mode]|1324}"] = "<Assistant_Title1>【Story Mode】</>\n<Assistant_Title2> System Settings: </>Menu-Settings-Camera-Story Mode{JumpToUI:[【Go to View】]|1302534}\n<Assistant_Title2> System Introduction: </>After Story Mode is enabled, the camera will zoom in to a cinematic perspective within story instances to enhance immersion. You can manually toggle it on/off by clicking the switch under the camera button on the bottom left of the screen, or permanently disable it in <Highlight>Settings-Camera-Story Mode-Enable Story Mode Dynamically</>. Once disabled, Story Mode will not activate when entering story instances again (except for some combat scenes).\n<Assistant_Title3> Recommended Searches: </>{SendAnswer:[Hiding Appearance in Story Mode]|1324}",
